cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the accompanying paper."
title: "cpi-coding-repro: reproducibility package for coding retail product names to consumer-price categories"
abstract: >-
  A fully synthetic, reproducible benchmark and evaluation code for coding
  short retail product names to consumer-price categories, accompanying
  arXiv:2606.02004. Includes a synthetic receipt-name generator for six
  COICOP-like categories, a trie pre-classifier, per-category binary
  confirmation models (bag-of-words and character n-gram logistic regression,
  an MLP, a CNN and an LSTM under one matched protocol), a learning-curve
  analysis, and a Monte-Carlo validation of the reliability-weighted
  consensus-labeling rule against majority vote and Dawid-Skene. Release 2.0.0
  matches the training budget across model families: the convolutional and
  recurrent models previously ran for a fixed eight epochs while every other
  model ran to its own convergence criterion, and they now stop on the same
  loss-improvement rule, which changes their reported accuracy. It also adds a
  computational cost benchmark (training time, inference throughput, model
  size, peak memory) and robustness checks covering the training budget, the
  decision threshold, the measurement batch size, and batch against online
  label aggregation. Release 1.1.0 remains the version that reproduces the
  numbers of arXiv:2606.02004v3. Contains no proprietary or production data.
